    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39024" root="موث" body-key="m">
    
      1 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَاثَ</span></b> , aor. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يَمُوثُ</span>, inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَوْثٌ</span> (and in the
CK <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَوَثٌ</span>) and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَوَثَانٌ</span>; (S, K;) as also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَاثَ</span>,
aor. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يَمِيثُ</span>; (TA;) and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اماث</span></b> ; (Hr;) but this
is disapproved by IAth; <i>He steeped</i> a thing <i>in
water, and mashed</i> it <i>with his hand:</i> (TA:) <i>he
mixed and moistened</i> a thing in water. (S, K.)
[See also art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ميث</span>.] ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  See also 7. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ماثَتِ الأَرْضُ</span>
<i>The land became soft and even.</i> (Msb.)

